JS — async generator with backpressure overruns memory.

```javascript
async function* fetchAll(urls) {
  const results = await Promise.all(urls.map(fetch));
  for (const r of results) yield r;
}
```

Bug: `Promise.all` waits for every fetch before yielding any — the generator buffers all responses in memory, defeating the whole point of streaming.

Fix:
```javascript
async function* fetchAll(urls) {
  for (const u of urls) {
    yield await fetch(u);
  }
}
```

Fetching one at a time and yielding immediately limits memory to one response at a time; pair with a concurrency-limit helper if parallelism is needed without the buffering.
